    "style": "barrel front Mediterranean Revival",
    "note": "An example of the barrel front Mediterranean Revival house: a bowed bay projecting over the garage under a shaped or crenellated parapet capped with Spanish tile. This was the standard Sunset District house from the mid-1920s until about 1931, and the crash ended it. Significance in this type comes from a whole run of them together rather than from any one house."
